s, child support, disability), they are often insufficient to lift people out of poverty, and many who need help fall through the cracks due to bureaucratic barriers. 8. **Health and Education Challenges**: The HIV/AIDS epidemic and tuberculosis have devastated households, while the education system still fails to provide quality schooling for most Black children, perpetuating the cycle of poverty. In short, while apartheid legally ended, its economic and social architecture remains largely intact. Overcoming that requires not just redistribution but sustained, inclusive growth, institutional reform, and targeted policies to address the multifaceted nature of poverty.
